  Patience.

  With that wand so close?  

  IME, there's usually a boulder on the left side of the Castle.  It's
not always in a usable position, though.  (Now I hope you see the
value of Sokoban.)

  See:
  <http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/medusa.html#cross>

  Review all possible techniques until you've got them memorized.
That way you'll recognize a solution when it presents itself.  I.e.
Kill giants so that any boulder they might possibly drop will be in a
useful position.


  It shouldn't be too long before a monster drops something that will
let you use one of those techniques.

  Come to think of it, did you break the statues in Medusa?

  Anything that can get you across medusa can definitely get you
across a single water square.  

  There's always the last chance solution:  Let a monster break the
drawbridge somehow.  (Although if you've a wand of digging you might
be able to do that now.) Kill monsters across moat with rocks (see why
there are so many statues to break into nice rocks at Medusa?).
Or use pole arms.  

  Then remove all rustables and put into bag of holding.  Repeat: Bag
of *holding*.  Don't try this with any other kind of bag.  Throw bag
of holding across moat into Castle.  Test to be *sure* you can throw
the BoH that far.  Then start stepping into the moat in front of the
drawbridge.  At some point you'll end up in the Castle.


  When I say last ditch approach, I mean it.  Don't do that if there's
any other way.  And I'd almost bet you already have another way, you
just don't know it.  For instance, check your spells: jumping, cone of
cold, etc.


  Give up indeed.



